pub(forged)           [def head pattern]            {:raised, FunctionClauseError}
nested(%{item: forged}) [defp head pattern]         {:raised, FunctionClauseError}
mapped([forged])        [defp via &priv/1]          {:raised, FunctionClauseError}
leak().(forged)         [escaped defp]              {:raised, FunctionClauseError}
nested_loose(%{item: forged}) [defp, no pattern]    {:ok, 100}
pub(%Order{total: 5}) [control]                     {:ok, 5}
--- compile-time: does 1.14 warn about a defp that accepts a wider type than its callers pass? (no type checker in 1.14)
elixir 1.14.0
